Incidentally, this brings up the following:  I started with two wild caught individuals to produce the F1.  I am using SNPs and I know what the genotype in the F1 is for all markers (otherwise they would not be in the data.  I am not exactly clear how I can make data where each SNP has 2 alleles and the possible genotypes (genomewise) are

'AA','AC','AG','AT','CC','CG','CT','GG','GT','TT'

into

"For a 4-way cross, the mother and father are assumed to have genotypes AB and CD, respectively. The genotype data for the progeny is assumed to be phase-known, with the following coding scheme: NA = missing, 1 = AC, 2 = BC, 3 = AD, 4 = BD, 5 = A = AC or AD, 6 = B = BC or BD, 7 = C = AC or BC, 8 = D = AD or BD, 9 = AC or BD, 10 = AD or BC, 11 = not AC, 12 = not BC, 13 = not AD, 14 = not BD."

Cheers

F

